        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bear Lane, Christ Church, Oxford, Bear Inn, Oxford, Alfred Street, Blue Boar Street, Oxford, England\n- Organizations: University of Oxford\n- Concepts: Latin names\n\nFacts:\n- Christ Church, Oxford, is a constituent college of the University of Oxford in England.\n- Christ Church, Oxford, has the Latin name \"Ædes Christi,\" meaning the temple or house of Christ, and it is sometimes known as \"The House.\"\n- Bear Lane is located just north of Christ Church, Oxford.\n- The circa-17th-century Bear Inn, Oxford, stands on the corner of Alfred Street and Blue Boar Street in central Oxford.\n- The Bear Inn, Oxford, stands opposite Bear Lane and just north of Christ Church, Oxford.",
